    "title": "Sevierville Firm Grabs Two Gay Street Buildings After Ephant Group's Collapse - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Tyler Evans ,\n8 hours ago Two of downtown Knoxville's most talked-about Gay Street properties have new owners once again, after Sevierville-based Compass Ventures purchased 304 and 308 S. Gay St. at a foreclosure auction on July 31. The sale marks the second time the vacant lot at 308 S. Gay St. has changed hands since 2020, and it closes a rough chapter for Ephant Group, the previous owner whose downtown ambitions stalled amid financial trouble. Read full article",
